        "bodyTr": "President Lee Jae-myung has announced he will strengthen direct communication with the public through social media regarding key issues facing the nation. Despite concerns from some within the ruling camp about the negative effects of excessive SNS use, the president's commitment to SNS engagement is expected to expand further. The president stated he will continue visiting back alleys to hear the voices of the marginalized, emphasizing that those with less need more attention and support than influential figures with greater resources. According to the Blue House, the president decided to expand direct public communication after witnessing Mexican President Claudia Sheinbaum hold press conferences four days a week and visit provincial areas three days a week during his recent state visit to Mexico.\n\nIt is difficult to fault the president for using SNS as a means to disseminate messages or for his commitment to communicate with citizens by visiting local communities. However, it is worth examining whether the specific manifestations of this approach align with his goal of becoming \"a president for everyone.\" The president stated he would accept opposing opinions but block comments containing insults or abusive language. Recently, critical comments on the president's posts have been primarily coming from progressive hardliners demanding stronger prosecutorial reform rather than from the conservative camp. The president's criticism of those who \"enjoy luxury at taxpayers' expense while cutting welfare budgets for ordinary people\" is widely seen as targeting hardliners within the ruling party. This has led to interpretations that the SNS enhancement initiative is actually focused on factional hegemony struggles within the coalition.\n\nA more fundamental issue is that while the president emphasizes SNS and communication, tangible policy achievements are not materializing. Real estate tax reform centered on regulations targeting ultra-luxury apartment owners has created side effects destabilizing housing security for ordinary citizens through jeonse shortages and soaring monthly rent prices. The agricultural land investigation policy, which has hit the brakes, has only spread anxiety in rural areas. The youth unemployment crisis, which is reaching historic lows, remains without meaningful solutions. It would be problematic if the president's enhanced communication becomes a tool for consolidating support within his faction or for dividing society between the haves and have-nots. Ultimately, administrations are evaluated on whether they solve the actual problems in people's lives.",
